that time you put c4 in just the right  spot and blew it when your teammates  shouted there on the stairs that time  you rappelled down the edifice of a  building and cleared out a defender from  a window upside down that time your plan  sucked in terrorist hunt and the last  thing you heard was the wheezy gasp of a  bomber just before half your team was  incinerated or that time a youtuber shot  the hostage in the face at the end of  round five just when you were about to  win oh my god he did it oh my god he  shut off the face what a monster The  Rainbow six siege beta that we previewed  last week was made up of these moments  siege is a tough tactical game with  Wiley AI and even while air human  opponents we're careful communicating  teams must plan execute and adapt or  pretty much get their asses handed to  them what we saw in this build of siege  were new operators attackers blitz IQ  and fuse and defenders doc bandit and  jager notes some people have already  seen doc two new maps consulate and  hereford base hosted rounds of TDM bomb  TDM hostage TDM secure area and PvE  disarm bomb and terrorist hunt classic  yes devs have dropped the taro hunt  slang probably because they were getting  too many tarot card SEO hits my overall  impression of the new operators were  that many of their gadgets aren't is  useful as the original roster and PvP  but rather seemed designed for the new  PvE modes for example jaegers active  defense device that stops incoming  grenades would actually hurt you in PvP  we're getting the enemy team to frag the  hostage is a legit winning strategy but  in the PvE disarm bomb mode where waves  of enemy AI breach room you're defending  could be the key to stopping enemy  grenades from overwhelming your fire  team my favorite new operator ended up  being blitz who's flash shield is  essentially an on-demand flashbang  grenade akin to how sledge has a  permanent breaching ability with his  hammer when it comes two modes Vegas  fans asked and ubi delivered with  terrorist hunt classic unlike disarm  bomb the new PvE mode has no side  objectives and teams go fold America on  a build  full of white masks bad guys it was this  mode that the enemy AI showed their  prowess by free roaming the map even  flanking outside the building to pick  off repelling operators  shuffle up that's job nice job when it  came to gunplay the weapons of siege  still feel a little too friendly for a  tactical shooter the ability of those  carrying shields to rapidly hit by our  pistols in particular felt wrong  shotguns on the other hand where the  stand out of this build by not falling  victim to the typical video game trope  and delivering stopping power at decent  range as a shotgun should not to mention  punching sweet peekaboo holes in walls  siege still needs to balance weapons a  little to discourage run-and-gun tactics  that could ruin its tactical aspects  that's what a beta is for our team coach  kept choosing IQ solely for her weapons  and at the end of the three-hour session  despite having wiped out the opposing  team several times by herself hadn't  cracked her electronics detector gadget  at the end of the day I had a great time  with the siege beta there's nothing  quite like coming up with a plan on the  fly and getting all the moving parts to  work each round felt like a small game  of shooter chess the catch is that  communication relies largely on people  talking a new evolved style spotting  mechanic great directional sound and the  ability for dead friendlies to use  surveillance cameras to spot enemies  have all reduced the need for chatting  but any team that's talking will  probably win talking and planning with a  team is both sieges greatest strength  and potentially greatest weakness I for  one will not be reaching for the usual  mute all button that is necessary to  tolerate playing so many other  multiplayer shooters we'll see what the  casual game is like when the beta drops  on sep tember 24th 